== Actual rho applicability
The audited public E6 model has j neither 0 nor 1728. Neither j nor its coefficients are fixed by p, p² or p³; all are fixed by p⁶. The prime-field sixfold module and bare proper-subfield Frobenius folds cannot be assumed applicable. This is not an exhaustive endomorphism/isogeny search or a rho trial. Known-j/singularity and original-point controls pass. [pcc:unverified]

== Why review the graph input, rather than only the root stage
On the exposed pair, removing all 398,639 root products leaves 1,029,748 of 1,428,387 partial products: an optimistic root-only factor ceiling of 1.3871. The current implementation already uses gcd(f,x^p-x). New normal forms and ideal updates would have to be charged. [pcc:unverified]

For H3 with k<=8 and 509 columns, at least 501 projected rows are necessary. The first recorded batch with that many is B=153600; the observed stop is B=155648. At most 2048 fewer B values could be examined within this recorded schedule. This is a row-count opportunity bound, not a CPU saving or an earlier rank certificate. Unadmitted rank 0 is not actual rank 0. [pcc:unverified]

